  "notes": "A formal, weighty word for loss. Typically used for significant, often irreversible losses — not for misplacing everyday objects. Commonly paired with abstract nouns like {記憶|きおく} (memory), {意識|いしき} (consciousness), {資格|しかく} (qualification), or {自信|じしん} (confidence).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {記憶|きおく}{喪失|そうしつ} — memory loss, amnesia\n- {意識|いしき}{喪失|そうしつ} — loss of consciousness\n- {資格|しかく}の{喪失|そうしつ} — forfeiture of qualifications\n- {喪失感|そうしつかん} — sense of loss",
